# BuildBarn — Operator Infrastructure Runbook (template)

> **DO NOT** rename this file to `INFRASTRUCTURE.md` and commit it. The
> repo-root `.gitignore` blocks `IaC/buildbarn/**/INFRASTRUCTURE.md`
> on purpose, but git is good at outsmarting itself. If you want to
> keep the live runbook in version control, store it in a private
> Percona repo, the corp password manager, or a Vault entry — anywhere
> that isn't this public-bound repository.
>
> Workflow:
>   `cp INFRASTRUCTURE.md.example INFRASTRUCTURE.md`
>   then fill in the placeholders below from your live deployment.
>   `INFRASTRUCTURE.md` will sit untracked in your local working copy
>   and survive `git pull` / `git checkout`.

This file complements `ondemand/compose/.env.example`. The `.env.example`
is the *form* (variable names + per-variable comments, all in one place
so docker-compose can source it). This file is the *map* — it pairs
each placeholder with where it appears in code/docs/Hetzner console and
why it's there. When you change something live, search this file first
to find every other place that needs the same edit.

---

## 1. Domain / DNS

| Placeholder | Live value (fill in) | Source / where set |
|---|---|---|
| `${PUBLIC_HOSTNAME}` | `____________________` | DNS A record (No-IP for dev) → `${PUBLIC_IP}`. Subject of the Let's Encrypt cert at `/etc/buildbarn/certs/fullchain.pem`. |
| `${LE_EMAIL}` | `____________________` | `certbot register --email …` — Let's Encrypt notifications. Use a Percona address (e.g. `builds-noreply@percona.com`); personal mail leaks into LE's public CT log. |

Migration trigger: when this graduates onto a Percona-owned domain, the
swap touches:
- DNS (point new hostname at the same Floating IP)
- Cert renewal hook (`certbot certonly … -d <new>`)
- `${PUBLIC_HOSTNAME}` in `.env`
- Dex `oidcIssuer` (`compose/dex/dex.yaml`) and OAuth callback URL on
  GitHub
- All redirect URIs registered in `dex.yaml::staticClients[].redirectURIs`

## 2. Hetzner Cloud project

| Placeholder | Live value (fill in) | Where it appears |
|---|---|---|
| `${HCLOUD_PROJECT_NAME}` | `____________________` | Hetzner console > Projects |
| `${HCLOUD_TOKEN}` | `(in .env only)`     | Project > Security > API tokens. Read+write on servers, networks, SSH keys. |
| `${HCLOUD_NETWORK_ID}` | `____________________` | `hcloud network list -o noheader -o columns=id,name`. Numeric ID workers join on spawn. |
| `${HCLOUD_NETWORK_NAME}` | `____________________` | Same query, name column. Used in Hetzner console UI navigation. |
| `${HCLOUD_NETWORK_CIDR}` | `____________________` | `hcloud network describe ${HCLOUD_NETWORK_ID}`. The `/16` your private IPs come from. |

## 3. Central VM

| Placeholder | Live value (fill in) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `${CENTRAL_VM_NAME}` | `____________________` | `hcloud server list` |
| `${CENTRAL_VM_TYPE}` | `____________________` | e.g. cpx41. Influences how many workers you can colocate; doesn't affect auth. |
| `${CENTRAL_PUBLIC_IP}` | `____________________` | Primary IPv4 of the VM. **Rotates** on VM redeploy — do NOT bake into anything stable. |
| `${PUBLIC_IP}` (Floating) | `____________________` | Hetzner Floating IP attached to the central VM. The DNS A-record points HERE. Stable across VM redeploy; €1/mo. |
| `${PRIVATE_IP}` | `____________________` | Address in `${HCLOUD_NETWORK_CIDR}`. Workers dial scheduler at `${PRIVATE_IP}:8983` and frontend at `${PRIVATE_IP}:8980`. |

